<title>USA: KAL jet may have had fire on board - U.S. officials.</title>
<headline>KAL jet may have had fire on board - U.S. officials.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>White House officials said on Tuesday there were unconfirmed reports that the pilot of the Korean Air Lines aircraft that crashed on Guam had radioed of the possibility of a fire on board before the plane went down.</p>
<p>&quot;The pilot reportedly declared an in-flight emergency because of a possible fire on board,&quot; said one official, who asked not to be identified. Another official stressed that the information was &quot;unconfirmed.&quot;</p>
</text>
